<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75647" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀστρᾰκ-όω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>turn into potsherds, dash to pieces</i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be dashed in pieces</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				180.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>make</i> the skin <i>hard like shell</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀ. τὸ δέρμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					869b25
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>become covered with a hard shell</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				89
			</span></i>; so of bread baked to a crust, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.50
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>pave with concrete</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀστρακοκονία</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.463.82
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv B. C.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
